      "text": "1. The first step is to identify the angles in the figure.\n2. The sum of the three angles at points A and C is 180 degrees since they form a right angle.\n3. The angle at point B is 55 degrees, and the angle at point D is 75 degrees.\n4. Now, to find the unknown angle at point B, subtract the sum of the angles at A and C from 180 degrees: \n   180 - (55 + 75) = 50 degrees.\n5. Similarly, to find the unknown angle at point D, subtract the sum of the angles at B and C from 180 degrees:\n   180 - (55 + 50) = 75 degrees.\n6. So, the angles around point B form a 50 degree and a 75 degree angle, and the angles around point D form a 50 degree and a 75 degree angle.\n7. The length of segment BC is the sum of the three segments from angles A, B, and C: BR + RB + CB = 60.\n8. Thus, the length of segment CD is the sum of the three points from angles B, C, and D: SSB + SB + CB = 80.\n9. Therefore, the longest segment is the one that corresponds to the greatest sum of angles, which is segment CD = \\boxed{CD}.",
